# Graph eval set — docgen
#
# Eight questions retrieval cannot answer. The first three are the ones Module 2 left
# deliberately broken; the rest push the same three shapes harder.
#
# Each entry names the traversal that should answer it, so this measures whether your GRAPH
# holds the facts — not how the agent phrases things. `<` before a relation traverses it
# backwards; `then` continues from a filtered set.
{"id": "GQ1", "shape": "multi-hop", "q": "Which projects were waiting on Atlas Migration to finish?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "project:atlas", "path": ["<depends_on"]}, "expect": ["project:cirrus", "project:halo"], "why": "One hop, but neither dependency appears in any status update: Cirrus's is in its own charter and Halo's only in the steering minute of 2026-07-16. Similarity search on 'Atlas' returns status updates, which name neither."}
{"id": "GQ2", "shape": "aggregation", "q": "How many milestones slipped across the programme?", "op": {"kind": "nodes", "type": "Milestone", "filter": {"prop": "slipped", "op": "eq", "value": true}}, "expect": ["ms:atlas-cutover", "ms:cirrus-live", "ms:observability-scoping"], "why": "Exactly three, reported in three different monthly files. The complete set exists in no single document, and top-k returns the most similar few."}
{"id": "GQ3", "shape": "temporal", "q": "Was the reporting views migration in Atlas's scope in April 2026?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "project:atlas", "path": ["has_version", "in_scope"], "as_of": "2026-04-15", "filter": {"prop": "id", "op": "eq", "value": "scope:reporting-views"}}, "expect": ["scope:reporting-views"], "why": "Yes under version 1. Both charter versions are in ONE file, so no chunking separates them and no per-file flag can retire one — the answer is in the validity dates, not the text."}
{"id": "GQ4", "shape": "temporal", "q": "Is the reporting views migration in Atlas's scope now?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "project:atlas", "path": ["has_version", "in_scope"], "as_of": "2026-09-13", "filter": {"prop": "id", "op": "eq", "value": "scope:reporting-views"}}, "expect": [], "why": "No — descoped 2026-05-14. The same traversal as GQ3 with a different date and the opposite answer."}
{"id": "GQ5", "shape": "aggregation", "q": "Who owns a milestone that slipped?", "op": {"kind": "nodes", "type": "Milestone", "filter": {"prop": "slipped", "op": "eq", "value": true}, "then": ["<has_milestone", "owned_by"]}, "expect": ["person:dana", "person:lena", "person:priya"], "why": "The second half of the aggregation question: select the set, then hop to the owners. Dana appears because ownership of the Observability Programme was taken on 2026-08-26 — before that it was unassigned, which the graph records as a person rather than a missing edge."}
{"id": "GQ6", "shape": "aggregation", "q": "Which projects have no open risk against them?", "op": {"kind": "coverage", "type": "Project", "missing_rel": "risk_against", "direction": "in"}, "expect": [], "why": "None — every project carries at least one risk. An empty answer that is CORRECT, which is worth showing: the shape of the query is right even though the set is empty, and a retriever returning nothing looks identical to a retriever that failed."}
{"id": "GQ7", "shape": "multi-hop", "q": "Which projects are affected by a change request that Lena raised?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "person:lena", "path": ["<raised_by", "affects"]}, "expect": ["project:cirrus"], "why": "Two hops, one backwards. Both of Lena's change requests affect Cirrus, so the complete set has one member — and a count of change requests would have said two."}
{"id": "GQ8", "shape": "multi-hop", "q": "Which project exists only because something was descoped from Atlas?", "op": {"kind": "reach", "start": "project:atlas", "path": ["<affects", "establishes"]}, "expect": ["project:halo"], "why": "CR-12 affects Atlas and establishes Halo. The causal chain from a descope to a new project is three documents apart: the charter says what was descoped, the CR register says what became of it, and the minutes say when it entered the programme."}
